The Evolution of System Administration
========================================================================================
Traditional IT Environment

Years ago, organizations had:

5 Servers
10 Servers
Small Infrastructure

A System Administrator could manually:

Create users
Install software
Apply patches
Restart services
Configure applications

Everything was manageable.
=============================================================================================
Modern IT Environment

Today's organizations may have:

100 Servers
500 Servers
5000 Servers
Containers
Cloud Instances
Kubernetes Clusters

Infrastructure changes every day.

Servers are:

Created automatically
Destroyed automatically
Scaled automatically

Manual administration is no longer practical.

The Challenge

Imagine:

A company has 500 Linux servers.

Management asks:

Install Apache on all servers before 6 PM.

Possible manually?

Technically yes.

Practically no.

This is where automation becomes essential.
============================================================================================================
What is Ansible?

Ansible is an Open Source IT Automation Platform.

It helps automate:

Configuration Management
Application Deployment
Infrastructure Provisioning
Orchestration
Security Compliance
Cloud Management
Developed By

Originally developed by:

Ansible, Inc.

Later acquired by:

Red Hat

Simple Definition

Ansible is a tool that allows one machine to manage and automate tasks across multiple machines.

Think of it as:

One Control Machine
        ↓
Many Target Servers
