Low learning curve
6. What is Configuration Management?

One of the most important concepts.

Definition

Configuration Management is the process of maintaining systems in a desired state.

Example

Organization Policy:

Every Linux server must have:

Nginx installed
SSH configured
Firewall enabled
Monitoring agent installed

Configuration Management ensures all servers follow these standards.

Benefits
Consistency
Standardization
Compliance
Faster recovery

