Core ConceptsTo grasp Ansible, understand its key structural components:
Control Node: The central computer where Ansible is installed and commands are run.
Managed Nodes: The remote servers, network devices, or cloud instances managed by the control node.
Agentless Architecture: Ansible does not require agent software on managed nodes; it connects securely over standard SSH (Linux) or WinRM (Windows).
Inventory File: A text file listing the hostnames or IP addresses of managed nodes.
Modules: Ready-to-use toolkits executing specific actions (e.g., installing packages, copying files) on target systems.
Playbooks: YAML-formatted configuration blueprints outlining multi-machine deployment workflows
